    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d471">

                <pb facs="0566" n="556" sameAs="frus:frus1944v02/pg556"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.796/10–1144: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-11T10:00:00+03:00">October 11,
                            1944—10 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 1:12 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3890. Re Department’s circular, October 7, midnight.<anchor n="93"
                        xml:id="d471-f1"/> I have not yet had a reply to my note of September 13
                    inviting the Soviet Government <pb facs="0567" n="557" xml:id="pg557"/> to send
                    a delegation to the Conference on Postwar Civil Aviation.</p>
                <p>I have written again requesting an early indication as to whether the Soviet
                    Government will find it possible to be represented at the Conference.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d471-f1" n="93" xml:id="d471-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it contained detailed arrangements for the Aviation Conference
                    (800.796/10–744).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
